{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{# S78 step 7 — this page had its own <!DOCTYPE> and <head>. With no layout
   there was nowhere to put a stylesheet link, which is why every one of these
   grew a <style> and every <style> grew literal colours. The shell emits the
   doctype, style.css, the favicon and importmap('app'); this file keeps only
   what is its own.

   S84 — the list is a `_data_table` now and the 325-line inline block is gone:
   page chrome S82 unwound, a `.admin-panel` copy that **overrode S83's ground
   and lift**, a complete modal that is not in this page's markup, a
   `.users-table` ruleset for a `<table>` this page stopped having, and a
   15-track `grid-template-columns` with a `min-width: 1780px`.

   🔴 Found by the conversion: the status cell was `class="status-badge active"`
   **hardcoded**, so a banned or pending member printed their real word inside a
   green chip. The class comes off the value now. #}

{% block title %}{{ 'admin_users.browser_title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/admin.css') ~ '?v=20260901-s158' }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{# ⚠️ The tiles count `allUsers`, not `users` (S134h). `users` is the FILTERED
   result, so with a status selected every tile reported the number of rows
   already on screen — four tiles, one number, and nothing to say there were more
   accounts elsewhere. `allUsers` is also where "3 sur 11" comes from.

   ⚠️ The role menu is built with `keys|map`, not `map|values`. `roleChoices` is
   keyed by role value and `map` preserves keys, so merging its result into a list
   gives a hash with holes rather than a sequence — and this Twig has no `values`
   filter to flatten it back. Mapping over the KEYS is what returns a plain list.

   ⚠️ **Le filtre « groupe » (S158c) est le voisin du précédent, et il a la même
   raison de ne pas être une jointure** : l'appartenance est l'union des lignes
   stockées, des rôles et de l'audience `user` — seule cette dernière vaut « tout
   compte actif », et aucune jointure ne l'écrit. Il vient AVANT le forfait dans
   la rangée parce qu'un groupe organise des personnes et qu'un forfait leur
   donne des droits : on cherche d'abord qui, ensuite quoi.

   ⚠️ **Le filtre « droit d'usage » (S153c), et sa clé est un ID.** Il ne se
   règle PAS dans `findForAdminFilters()` : `USAGE_RIGHT_ASSIGNMENT` n'a pas
   d'entité, donc rien à joindre en DQL, et surtout l'appartenance à un groupe
   n'est pas une jointure — c'est l'union de lignes stockées, de rôles et de
   l'audience `user`, que `AudienceResolver` seul sait résoudre. Le contrôleur
   filtre donc la liste après coup, en passant par lui.
   ⚠️ Le menu ne s'affiche que s'il existe au moins un package : un `<select>` à
   une seule entrée « Tous » est un contrôle qui ne fait rien.
   ⚠️ **Les tuiles et « 3 sur 11 » comptent toujours `allUsers`**, donc le total
   reste celui du lab. C'est voulu : le compte de gauche dit combien la sélection
   montre, celui de droite combien il y a.

   ⚠️ Kept out of the argument hash: a comment between two of its keys is a Twig
   syntax error. #}
{% embed 'site/_admin_list.html.twig' with {
    action_label: 'admin_users.action_label'|trans,
    action_route: 'app_admin_user_new',
    panel_title: 'admin_users.panel_title'|trans,
    panel_note: 'admin_users.panel_note'|trans({'count': users|length}),
    list_count: users|length,
    list_total: allUsers|length,
    list_route: 'app_admin_users',
    list_search: filters.q|default(''),
    list_search_placeholder: 'common.search_placeholder'|trans,
    list_query: {statut: filters.statut, role: filters.role, package: filters.package, groupe: filters.groupe},
    list_tiles_label: 'admin_list.facet_status'|trans,
    list_tiles: [
        {label: 'admin_list.all'|trans, count: allUsers|length, query: {statut: ''}},
        {label: 'admin_list.active'|trans, count: allUsers|filter(user => user.statut == 'actif')|length, query: {statut: 'actif'}},
        {label: 'admin_list.inactive'|trans, count: allUsers|filter(user => user.statut == 'inactif')|length, query: {statut: 'inactif'}},
        {label: 'admin_list.pending'|trans, count: allUsers|filter(user => user.statut == 'pending')|length, query: {statut: 'pending'}},
    ],
    list_refine: [
        {name: 'role', label: 'workspace.filter.role'|trans, value: filters.role, options: [{value: '', label: 'admin_list.all'|trans}]|merge(roleChoices|keys|map(value => {value: value, label: roleChoices[value]}))},
    ]|merge(groupChoices|length > 0 ? [
        {name: 'groupe', label: 'admin_users.filter_group'|trans, value: filters.groupe, options: [{value: '', label: 'admin_list.all'|trans}]|merge(groupChoices|map(g => {value: g.id, label: g.label}))},
    ] : [])|merge(packageChoices|length > 0 ? [
        {name: 'package', label: 'admin_users.filter_package'|trans, value: filters.package, options: [{value: '', label: 'admin_list.all'|trans}]|merge(packageChoices|map(p => {value: p.id, label: p.name}))},
    ] : []),
} %}
    {% block content %}
        {# ⚠️ The actions column and its link say "Voir", not "Modifier". Both said
           Modifier and both go to `app_admin_user_detail`, which is a detail page —
           its inline forms set a person type and validate a physical training,
           there is no edit form for the account. The page's own subtitle was
           corrected earlier; the label promising the edit was not.

           ⚠️ The note sits here rather than beside the column it describes,
           because a Twig comment between two keys of an argument hash is a syntax
           error. Both of this file's lint failures on the way to CT 210 were this
           note, not the change: first for that placement, then for spelling the
           comment-closing sequence inside a comment, which ends it early. #}
        {% embed 'site/_data_table.html.twig' with {
            pin_actions: true,
            columns: [
                {label: 'admin_users.col_member'|trans, class: 'is-grow'},
                {label: 'admin_users.col_status'|trans, class: 'is-tight'},
                {label: 'admin_users.col_progressions'|trans, class: 'is-tight'},
                {label: 'admin_users.col_rfid_logs'|trans, class: 'is-tight'},
                {label: 'common.see'|trans, class: 'is-actions'},
            ],
            rows: users,
            empty: 'admin_users.empty'|trans,
        } %}
            {% block rows %}
                {% for user in users %}
                    {% set logCount = logCounts[user.id]|default(0) %}
                    <tr data-admin-list-filter-row data-admin-list-filter-category="{{ (user.statut ?? '')|lower|replace({' ': '-'}) }}" data-admin-list-filter-row-href="{{ path('app_admin_user_detail', {id: user.id}) }}">
                        <td>{% include 'site/_cell_title.html.twig' with {
                            title: user.displayName,
                            href: path('app_admin_user_detail', {id: user.id}),
                            subtitle: user.email,
                            media: include('site/_cell_media.html.twig', {
                                initials: (user.firstName ?? user.username)|slice(0, 1) ~ (user.lastName ?? '')|slice(0, 1),
                                shape: 'circle',
                            }, with_context = false),
                        } only %}</td>
                        {# 🔴 Was `status-badge active` whatever the value (S84), and then
                           printed the stored word itself. `Utilisateur::getStatusKey()` is
                           the one mapping — see the entity. #}
                        {# 🔴 Was `class="status-badge {{ user.statut }}"` — the STORED WORD
                           interpolated into a class name, so a value no stylesheet knew
                           about got no colour and the chip stayed green whatever it said.
                           `_cell_state` takes a signal; the mapping is written here, once,
                           where it can be read. #}
                        {% set statusKey = user.statusKey %}
                        <td>{% include 'site/_cell_state.html.twig' with {
                            label: statusKey|trans,
                            signal: (user.statut ?? '') == 'actif' ? 'go' : ((user.statut ?? '') == 'pending' ? 'caution' : ((user.statut ?? '') == 'banned' ? 'stop' : 'muted')),
                        } only %}</td>
                        <td class="is-numeric">{{ progressionCounts[user.id]|default(0) }}</td>
                        <td class="is-numeric"><a class="rfid-log-link" href="{{ path('app_admin_access_rfid_logs') }}">{{ logCount }}</a></td>
                        <td class="is-actions">{% include 'site/_cell_actions.html.twig' with {
                            actions: [{label: 'common.see'|trans, icon: 'view', href: path('app_admin_user_detail', {id: user.id})}],
                        } only %}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            {% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
